    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="0884" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/17: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-07T10:00:00+03:06">July 7, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. My 55, June 22, 5 p.m. Number of pilgrims to Mecca this year is estimated as
                    high as 50,000. Substantial numbers should begin arriving by end September and
                    rush will begin a month later.</p>
                <pb facs="0885" n="873" xml:id="pg873"/>
                <p>All 15 million riyals referred to in Cairo’s 861, May 11, 9 a.m. will be needed
                    to combat upward tendency of riyal resulting from receipt of promised gold and
                    influx of foreign currencies with pilgrims. A runaway riyal will cause
                    destitution among pilgrims and otherwise aggravate difficulties of local
                    government.</p>
                <p>Long range plan mentioned in Department’s 27, June 30, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >10</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d919-f1"/> should not be permitted to
                    distract attention from urgency of present needs.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d919-f1" n="71" xml:id="d919-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it was a private telegram between officials of the California
                    Arabian Standard Oil Company (Casoc) containing information as to the
                    Department’s interest and efforts in the direction of solving on a long-range
                    basis the Saudi Arabian fiscal problem by means of a plan of currency
                    stabilization (012.3/9605a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
